charlie: Okay. I've got a thing, and I've been working up to it since the lobby, so let me get all the way through.
charlie[thinking]: Every time I land somewhere, I text one word. "Landed." Every flight, since I was a kid. It's just what you do.
charlie: But it's never gone to the same person twice in a row. It goes to whoever's meeting me. Whoever's nearest. It moves, like everything.
